   "body": {
    "en": "*Subtraction* also works column by column. 0 − 0 = 0, 1 − 0 = 1, 1 − 1 = 0, and 0 − 1 needs a borrow: the column borrows 1 from the next column on the left, which is worth 2 here, so 0 − 1 becomes 10 − 1 = 1. Computers usually avoid borrowing altogether by adding the 2's complement of the number to be subtracted (next topic)."
   },
